    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Daniel Smith founded Mishicot in 1844 by erecting a sawmill after moving to Wisconsin from New York.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://vi.mishicot.wi.gov/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Mishicot was named after Chief Mishicott as a sign of respect for the leader of the local Potawatomi community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://vi.mishicot.wi.gov/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers of Mishicot and the surrounding farmlands came primarily from Germany, Bohemia, Switzerland, and Canada.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mishicot%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village of Mishicot features three historic churches founded by early residents, representing the Catholic, Lutheran, and Methodist faiths.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://vi.mishicot.wi.gov/history/"
    },
    {
